---
title: "share_object (Sui Move Concepts: Shared Object Creation)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_key: check obj has key ability
    q_check_key --> q_check_fresh: obj has key ability
    q_check_key --> q_abort_key: missing key ability
    q_check_fresh --> q_share: object is freshly created (not yet owned)
    q_check_fresh --> q_abort_owned: object already address-owned
    q_share --> q_set_shared: transfer::share_object(obj)
    q_set_shared --> [*]: object is now shared (accessible by anyone)

    q_abort_key --> [*]: abort - share_object requires key ability
    q_abort_owned --> [*]: abort - cannot share already-owned object

    note right of q_check_fresh
        INV-001: Object can only be shared if not already address-owned
        INV-002: Once shared, object cannot be made address-owned again
    end note

    note right of q_set_shared
        INV-003: Shared objects require consensus sequencing for access
        INV-004: Multiple transactions can access shared objects concurrently
        INV-005: Shared objects are mutable by any transaction
    end note
